#!/usr/bin/env bash
# UserPromptSubmit hook: plain stdout is added to Claude's context, so every
# prompt starts with a reminder to follow the request-log workflow.
[ -n "$REQUEST_LOG_HEADLESS" ] && exit 0  # inside the headless narrative run (headless-narrative.sh)
cat >/dev/null
cat <<'MSG'
Request-log workflow (.claude/skills/request-log/SKILL.md) for any prompt that asks for work: 1) save it verbatim as requests_and_response/<new-slug>/request.md with its start time (one folder per request: request.md, report.html and all its media); 2) write <slug>/report.html from report_template.html (request, understanding, interpretations) and publish it to the request-log artifact; 3) add the tasks and how each is verified, split for parallel execution; 4) add the numbered plan (each step single or parallel) - a hook blocks code edits until steps 2-4 are in the report; run log_step.py at each step (async hooks rebuild the log, no manual builds); 5) update the HTML and republish; 6) when done, add the execution summary, evidence, every error met with its cause, a root-cause why-chain and a prevention (or 'No errors.'), and 2-5 suggested follow-ups that carry the user's goal further, run the evidence-reviewer agent in the background (it writes its verdict into the report), set status done, fill the Task summary from the staged diff, ONE commit and push, then build_artifact.py and republish. Evidence (.claude/skills/ui-evidence/SKILL.md): UI changes -> capture_pages.py before (BEFORE any UI edit) and after, so every changed view has a before/after image; action-sequence or button/event behaviour changes -> record_flow.py with named checks of values the action must change (Playwright video -> GIF + <name>-checks.json; a FAIL blocks; review the GIF frames, never the video); pages.json `ready` instead of network idle. Pure questions: skip. Follow-ups: update the previous request's files and artifact entry.
MSG
